-- title:
--   Injectivity of the Lubin–Tate coordinate via a finite cover
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a complete discrete valuation domain $W_0$ that is adically complete for its maximal ideal, that maximal ideal being generated by $q$, together with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal. Let $F_0$ be a commutative formal group law over $k$ satisfying `IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`, i.e. with respect to the zero ideal its $q$-th iterate series is a unit multiple of its Drinfeld divisor at $(0,0)$. Let $R$ be a Noetherian local $W_0$-algebra, adically complete for its maximal ideal, with a surjection $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ of kernel $\mathfrak m_R$ compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, let $F$ be a commutative formal group law over $R$ whose coefficientwise image under $\mathrm{res}_R$ is $F_0$, and let $x_0, x_1 \in \mathfrak m_R$ be such that $F$ satisfies the Drinfeld-basis condition for $(\mathfrak m_R, q, x_0, x_1)$. Assume: (i) the universality of $(R, F, x_0, x_1)$ among Artinian local $W_0$-algebras $T$ with compatible surjection onto $k$, carrying a commutative formal group law $G$ lifting $F_0$ and a Drinfeld basis $(y_0, y_1)$ in $\mathfrak m_T$ — there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : R \to T$ lifting the residue maps, together with a base change of $F$ along $\varphi$ and an isomorphism of laws onto $G$ whose series has coefficients reducing to $\delta_{n,1}$ and which sends the adic evaluations of $\varphi x_0, \varphi x_1$ to $y_0, y_1$; (ii) a commutative formal group law $F^{\mathrm u}$ over $W_0[[t]]$ lifting $F_0$ along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ \mathrm{constantCoeff}$, with the analogous universality among Artinian lifts of $F_0$ without level structure; (iii) a $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : W_0[[t]] \to R$ lifting residue maps, a base change $F'$ of $F^{\mathrm u}$ along $\varphi$ and an isomorphism of laws $F' \cong F$ with series reducing to $t$; (iv) a local $W_0[[t]]$-algebra $C$, finite as a module, adically complete, with compatible surjection onto $k$ of kernel $\mathfrak m_C$, carrying the base change $G^c$ of $F^{\mathrm u}$ and a Drinfeld basis $(c_0, c_1)$ in $\mathfrak m_C$, and with $W_0[[t]] \to C$ injective. Then $\varphi$ is injective.
--
--   This is the dominance step for the Lubin–Tate coordinate: the map from the power series ring parametrising deformations of $F_0$ into the deformation ring with Drinfeld level structure has zero kernel, deduced by reduction along the Artinian quotients of a finite cover $C$ representing Drinfeld bases together with Krull separation. It is used by [`FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.injective_algHom_powerSeries_of_universal`](thm.html#FormalGroup.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic.injective_algHom_powerSeries_of_universal), where the cover is produced rather than assumed.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FormalGroup_IsDrinfeldBasisAdic_injective_algHom_powerSeries_of_universal_of_cover.lean

